# CP2102N safety requirements

- Read `docs/PROTOCOL.md` before changing USB requests or config offsets.
- CP2102N uses full-block `GetConfig`/`SetConfig`; never replace this with
  legacy `CP210x_SetSerialNumber`.
- Treat the config as OTP. Minimize writes and never add automatic retries.
- Refuse writes unless config size is 678, version is 1, and
  `enableConfigUpdate` is `0xff`.
- Preserve every config byte except the serial area and checksum.
- Recalculate Fletcher-16 and verify the full config by reading it back.
- Never lock the configuration or change byte 4.
- Keep user selection interactive; never program all connected devices.
- Add or update tests for protocol, descriptor, checksum, and reset changes.
- Do not test writes on physical hardware unless the user explicitly asks.
